                      *** MoveFiles v0.3 ***

        AmiExpress Utility to move files older than X  days!
           Coded by Nameless, beta tested by Dalai Lama


Well, if you're getting tired of constantly filling up your BBS:Conf/Upload
directory with uploads, this program will quickly MOVE the files X nr of days
old, and older, from your upload directory to an archive path (From which ya
can move 'em offline to tape...) and at the same time update your
BBS:Conf/DirX files to reflect that they're no longer RECENT uploads.

All Parameters are set in a CONFIG file. The name of which is passed as an
argument to this program. I recommend you name the config file(s) the same
as your BBS:Conference to make it easy for ya to move those files (ya just
type 'MoveFiles BBS:ConfName' and it'll move the older stuff...


*** COMMAND SYNTAX ***


  MoveFiles  ConfigFile[.mfcnfg]  [QUICK]


WHERE:

ConfigFile  Is the name of the config file with the following options,
            If you don't understand - see the SAMPLE.MFCnfg file included.
            Note: the .mfcnfg is optional (it WILL append it if u didn't)

   NR_DAYS_OLD   xxx   <-(the number of days of files you want to keep)
   SRC_DIR_TXT   xxx   <-(source BBS:Conf/DirX text file path&name)
   SRC_PATH      xxx   <-(source BBS:Conf/Upload directory path)
   DEST_DIR_TXT  xxx   <-(destination BBS:Conf/DirX text file path&name)
   DEST_PATH     xxx   <-(destination archive dir path to move files to)


[QUICK]    Is an optional switch which turns OFF verbose mode (avoids the
           detailed info during run). With QUICK you will just be told
           to wait while processing, and It'll probably be slightly quicker.


*** CONSIDERATIONS ***


There is an assumptions that was made in doing this utility, which has to do
with your source & destination BBS:Conf/DirX text files. Most of you have been
modifyin' the heck out of yours so I thought ya ought to know:

  This utility assumes ALL DATES are in order from oldest (top) to newest
  (bottom) in both the source & destination text files. This version does
  not sort these files (maybe a later version will).  Failure to keep your
  dates in this order will prevent this utility from working correctly (It'll
  stop copying when it finds a date closer to the X number of days you
  specified). Note: there's a util called 'Arrange' by AirWolf which will
  sort your DirX files (just in case you've been mixing the dates up...)

INVALID dates in the date field (you know - like the word 'DELETED!' instead
of '03-04-92') are OK (YES OK!) - This program will just ignore that line as
even having legit file. You got that? No date, No file will be moved. Dates
are pretty important - hehe.

I also wanted to mention that header lines (at the top of the DirX file) are
ok, as long as you don't have a valid date in the date field - then It'll
think that line contains an actual filename to process.  When this program
updates the DirX files, it should ignore the headers.

Another thing to keep in mind is, IF it can't MOVE any of the upload files,
then it won't bother to try to update your DirX files. What I mean by that
is the program MUST succeed in actually transfering 1 file from your source
to your destination THEN it will update your dest DirX file with ALL of the
older files which were (OR were supposed to be) moved.


*** REVISION HISTORY ***


v0.1 - 5/12/92 - Initial release...beta for dalai lama to test out... bugs?
                 hmmm, none that I'm aware of in the brief time I checked
                 it out!
v0.2 - 5/13/92 - Rewrote copy function - 300% faster yeah! Changed link opts,
                 Eliminated ALL stdio functions for Amiga2.0.lib functions
                 Eliminated redundant functions, reduced size by 5K! I did
                 increase allocated buffer size, if you dont have at least
                 the memory to hold your source DirX text file + 100k this
                 program may choke and run out of memory. beta test release.
v0.3 - 5/17/92 - Fixed a bug which caused dest file to be deleted before
                 checking to see if source file existed. Also fixed bug with
                 memory alignment, changed malloc() to exec.library
                 AllocVec(). Reduced size another 1K. Added a skip of DirX
                 re-writes if no files were moved. Removed opening of
                 dos.library, done by link to c.o. Other minor cleanups...
                 ----->>>  Initial 'RaZorMaID GRouP' release!  <<<---


*** PLANNED/POSSIBLE IMPROVEMENTS ***


o  Had a suggestion to check for an '*' character right after the date (you
   know ... MM-DD-YY* ... and if it exists to delete that file from the upload
   dir and the text file without bothering to transering it.  Would make it
   easy to identify and get rid of 'lame' files, as well as those already
   backed up.

o  Had another suggestion to sort the DirX file (That would eliminate one of
   the current limitations - see above 'assumptions...'). If you know you're
   DirX file dates aren't sorted correctly by date - just use the Arrange Util
   by AirWolf. (if you can find it - hehe).


*** RELEASE INFO & COMMENTS ***


Last week, I was asked by a friend to code this utility, I havn't seen another
utility like this, so I figured a quick 'C' util would do it. I've spent a lot
of time assuring the safety (making sure NO DAMAGE) will come to any of your
files during run (I think this program is 80% error handling and 20% actual
code - hehe), but still, run at your own risk!. Anyway, I'd like to mention, I
do have the SAS C v5.1b SOURCE code available for ANYONE who wishes to examine
it (make sure it's ok), re-compile it..., or even modify it to suit their own
needs. Just call my board, Snarfs Pub (407)267-8155, and leave me a message
that ya want the code.

Lastly, I am running this under workbench v2.04, And I CAN'T guarantee that
it'll work under 1.3 - but I'm pretty sure it will. USE AT YOUR OWN RISK!

Later dudes, Nameless
